<.shell title="Milestone list" current={:milestone_list}>
  <h1>Milestone list</h1>
  <p class="lead">What a member reached, and the day.</p>

  <div class="demo max-w-md">
    <.milestone_list
      id="milestone-list-demo"
      milestones={SampleData.milestones()}
      today={~D[2026-10-12]}
    />
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>
    A member's milestones, all of them, on Your membership. The member sidebar a team admin sees shows only the latest, as text, and the team's Milestones page is a table.
  </p>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <p>Anything with a goal still to reach. Milestones are only what a member did.</p>

  <h2>Every milestone</h2>
  <p>
    Three kinds, each with its own icon. The lines below are the app's own, up to a little past what a long-serving member reaches; after that, hours go every 1,000, years every 5, and incidents every 100.
  </p>
  <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
    <div :for={
      {kind, heading} <- [
        {:hours, "Hours: a clock"},
        {:years, "Years on the team: a cake"},
        {:incidents, "Incidents: a lifebuoy"}
      ]
    }>
      <h3>{heading}</h3>
      <div class="demo">
        <.milestone_list
          id={"milestone-list-every-#{kind}"}
          milestones={SampleData.every_milestone(kind)}
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>New and earlier</h2>
  <p>
    One reached in the last 30 days gets a green New tag, <code>&lt;.badge kind=&#123;:success&#125;&gt;</code>. Every icon stays grey: a
    <code>--text-muted</code>
    icon in a <code>--surface-alt</code>
    circle. The word says why the row stands out; colour alone read as "special", and amber already means expiring on Your membership (decided 2026-10-23). No levels or confetti.
  </p>
  <div class="demo max-w-md">
    <.milestone_list
      id="milestone-list-new"
      milestones={SampleData.milestones()}
      today={~D[2026-10-26]}
    />
  </div>
  <p class="hint">
    Today is October 26, 2026 here: 25 incidents came 28 days ago, so it's new; 500 hours came 32 days ago, so it isn't.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul class="list">
    <li>
      Each row is what they reached, then the day and the activity that reached it. Years have no activity.
    </li>
    <li>
      The activity is plain text, not a link (decided 2026-10-23). Which activity tipped a total over a line is chance, and a link on every row would make the list look like something to open. The member's activities are a click away on their year page.
    </li>
    <li>Hours count every attended activity. Years leave out days in away periods.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.milestone_list id milestones today&gt;</code>
    with milestones from <code>MemberMilestones.for_member/3</code>, newest first, and today in the team's zone.
  </p>
</.shell>
